## StemLab matching before choosing rhythmic motion

- Standing instruction from Kieran, 11 October 2026: use StemLab's native DanceRudiments matching tool to find candidate movements before selecting new or materially revised BPM-matched animation and visual effects, especially videos and song EPK pages. Follow `Z:\My Songs\Workflows\stemlab-rudiment-motion-selection.md` and invoke the verified `Z:\My Songs\Tools\StemLab.ps1` runtime. Reuse saved analysis/stems first; preserve canonical timing and approved choreography, report-specific windows/phase and scores, creative review, motion bounds, accessibility/lifecycle QA and exact publication approvals. Matching proposes movement; it does not approve content or prove whole-song/downbeat fit. Metadata-only EPK edits do not require a new search.

## Localised intermittent audio-timed effects

- Apply this localisation rule project-wide only to intermittent audio-reactive, BPM-synchronised, beat-matched or cue-timed effects in videos, Shorts, visualisers, EPKs, social assets and interactive pages: discrete accents, bursts, hits or other effects that appear and disappear between events.
- Effects that are continuously ongoing, or continuously ongoing throughout audio playback, are excluded from this localisation rule and may span the whole frame, page, viewport or scene. A continuous repeating motion remains excluded even when its parameters vary with the audio clock. Classify the actual effect lifecycle, not merely whether its timing repeats.
- Confine each intermittent effect to a clearly bounded visual subject or local region, such as one plane, trail, lyric, particle group, cloud bank, light pool, progress indicator or defined section of the frame. State its affected area and maximum extent in the implementation or render contract.
- Do not use intermittent audio accents to tint, brighten, darken, flash, pulse, grade or otherwise alter colour values across the entire frame, page, viewport or full-scene background, including low-opacity full-frame overlays. Keep global grading and exposure stable through those intermittent accents. A narratively required whole-scene transition must be a documented finite section transition with an accessible fallback, not a recurring intermittent beat accent.
- Verify intermittent effects using representative active and inactive frames or computed regions; reject clock-driven changes outside their declared local bounds. Do not reject a continuously ongoing effect solely because it is page-wide or repeating.
- This exemption does not waive reduced-motion preferences, flashing safety, text contrast/readability, keyboard and screen-reader usability, clipping/lifecycle checks, performance budgets, or DanceMoves graceful-degradation and recovery testing.

## Smoke, particle and glow clipping checks

- Apply this rule to every visual effect, sprite, animation, video, EPK and interactive page that contains smoke, fog, particles, glows, trails or other expanding/fading artwork.
- For the ordinary site's shared Header/Footer effects, follow `Z:\My Songs\Workflows\shared-site-template-effects.md`. Patch a fresh editor backup against the recorded public source fingerprint, run the shared-brand preservation and extent guards, and reject stale whole-template builders. Update the public authority only after persisted and public verification; keep pending candidates distinct.
- Before publishing or exporting, inspect the full effect lifecycle: appearance, maximum spread/scale, movement extremes and fade-out. Check desktop and narrow layouts, and placements near the top, bottom and side edges.
- Calculate or sample the transformed extent, including scale origins, translation, blur, shadow and texture alpha, against every clipping ancestor and the scene/viewport boundary. A container's nominal size is not proof that its animated contents fit.
- Reject a visible straight cut through a cloud, glow or particle group. Provide transparent padding, a soft zero-alpha boundary, smaller extent or inward drift near scene edges so visible content fades before reaching a hard clip. Keep intermittent effects within their declared local bounds. Continuously ongoing effects may be page-wide under the exemption above, but must still have explicit scene extents and pass edge/lifecycle checks; page-wide scope alone is not a clipping fix.
- Retain representative frames and the extent-check result in the task record. After any change to size, travel, scale, blur, timing or container layout, repeat the relevant maximum-extent and edge-placement checks. A successful script parse or static screenshot is not sufficient visual verification.

## Local reports and data

- Apply this rule to every chat, task, and scheduled job in this project.
- At the start of each job, inspect `Z:\My Songs` and identify the subfolders that may contain reports or data relevant to the task.
- Recursively inspect those relevant subfolders and their descendants for existing reports and data that could assist with the task, descending to a maximum depth of 255 directory levels, and use any relevant findings.
